<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_VeilFallPaneStrike.xml              TerminalBiomes · TWILIGHT_PANE_STRIKE_1
  ============================================================================
  danger pass D1 — "Veil-fall pane strike: the sky sheds." §5 C6 (ruled):
  "it can kill outright; the ~15 s shadow warning is the fairness."

  Same shape as this mod's other biome-scoped atmosphere-and-danger
  incidents (RUT_WalkerSurfacing.xml, RM_SteamDevilAppears.xml — read
  before writing this file): category Misc (keeps it out of the vanilla
  Storyteller's ThreatSmall/ThreatBig queues — this is the sea's own
  standing hazard, not a raid-shaped threat) + targetTags Map_PlayerHome
  (fires on the sea-floor pocket map exactly like those two already do) +
  allowedBiomes restricting it to RM_TwilightSea.

  baseChance/minRefireDays INVENTED, same "MTB-ish ~once per N days" idiom
  those two files' own headers explain — D1(a)'s own words, "once in a
  while," land between SteamDevil's baseChance 2/minRefireDays 5 (routine
  spectacle) and WalkerSurfacing's baseChance 1/minRefireDays 14 (rare
  sighting): this can kill, so it sits at the rarer end.

  workerClass RM_IncidentWorker_PaneStrike (this mod's own Source/, not the
  shared EnvironmentalHazards assembly — Twilight-only content).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RM_VeilFallPaneStrike</defName>
    <label>waveglass pane strike</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.TerminalBiomes.RM_IncidentWorker_PaneStrike</workerClass>
    <baseChance>1.2</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>9</minRefireDays>
    <allowedBiomes>
      <li>RM_TwilightSea</li>
    </allowedBiomes>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
